<title>POLAND: ALL POLISH WEEKLY GRAIN AUCTION PRICES FALL.</title>
<headline>ALL POLISH WEEKLY GRAIN AUCTION PRICES FALL.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices of wheat, rye and barley</p>
<p>fell during last week's grain auctions, the Polish Agriculture</p>
<p>Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to March 15  previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	54.23 zl/q	 54.27 zl/q	  -5.3 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  40.96 zl/q	 41.04 zl/q	  13.9 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     47.58 zl/q	 48.26 zl/q	  -0.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
